Ryan.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:46.840
31.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.200
Seventh year.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:54.020
The traditional balloons rise into the sun-bright sky, signal that the start is just moments

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.740
away.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:56.740
The crowd becomes still.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.240
Holman, Speedway President, speaks the words that bring the waiting to an end.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.270
Gentlemen, start your engines.

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:29.960
Year of work.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:39.490
plan ready after weeks of practice and tuning ready ready Tony Holman signals

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:50.180
for the pace lap to begin the fans come to their feet as 33 high-powered

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:55.450
machines began a parade lap around this the greatest racecourse in the world the

00:14:55.450 --> 00:15:00.000
cars pile out of the pit area onto the track to form the traditional 11 row

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:05.450
of three abreast. The back straightaway and the cars bunched together. The three

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:13.030
cars that belong in front are not in position. The first three cars had pulled

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:16.750
out of the pits ahead of the pace car and must get around the track and into

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:21.810
position before they cross the starting line. The third turn. The second row

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:26.980
drivers still in front are holding back the field waiting for Rathman, Collision and Reese.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:42.140
fourth turn and the front row cars squeeze around the pack and into their

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:47.840
starting places just in time they're ready for the start here they come and

00:15:47.840 --> 00:16:00.000
the race is on first turn Dick Brathman out in front and they

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:10.190
Elysian right behind him.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.690
Through the second turn, Elysian cuts below the white line,

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:19.040
but Rathman holds him off.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:23.810
Back stretch, Elysian is wheel to wheel with Rathman,

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.660
going into the third turn, he passes.

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.840
Look out, Elysian has lost control.

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:37.470
Low motion cameras capture panel counter turdling over Jimmy Reese.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:50.780
The track is blocked for the rest of the field.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:54.500
Three other cars spin to avoid the wrecks.

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.320
Watch it!

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:57.880
He's ran by two more.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:06.520
Look out! There goes another!

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:11.300
Seconds, a total of 14 battered racing machines litter the treacherous third turn.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:18.770
The remainder of the field work their way through the wreckage of the worst collision in speedway history.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:27.360
In the pits, mechanics are baffled. Their drivers should have come around long ago.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:34.730
Some of the cars are pushed clear of the track.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:37.050
Others must wait for the tow truck.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:40.230
Paul Russo brings his number 15 Novi Special into the pits

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:42.810
under its own power and reports to his crew

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.890
